    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense looks primed for a productive slate today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who anchor our projections with scores of 81.88 and 73.23, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** is our most compelling play; he benefits from a premier matchup against Painter (xERA 4.67) and a massive 16% park factor boost, effectively nullifying the minor drag created by the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is the beneficiary of a strong platoon advantage against the right-handed Elder, whose 4.28 xERA provides a clear runway for production. We are also leaning heavily on **Sam Antonacci** (65.85) at the top of the order; despite a park penalty, his leadoff placement and favorable platoon status against Nick Martinez make him a high-floor asset as we continue to prioritize speed and efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Jorge Polanco**, who missed the cut with a 50.55 score. While **Jorge Polanco** remains a reliable depth piece, his lower projected efficiency\u2014hampered by a subpar batting order position\u2014made him the odd man out compared to the raw scoring output of **Coby Mayo** and **Kyle Tucker**. Risk management is also a focal point today; **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** face a stiff challenge against Suarez, whose 3.48 xERA demands caution. Furthermore, we are keeping a close watch on **Miguel Vargas**, who, despite a decent 55.80 score, faces a specific risk from Nick Martinez\u2019s tendency to control the base paths, potentially stifling our stolen base upside. We remain without **Jordan Westburg** due to his IL status, leaving our infield rotation reliant on the sustained health of our core starters.",
